      "internal": false,
      "mergeID": "6ac7d9d6ed93e5dacc95a8d4",
      "mergedPostDetails": "A very basic feedback feature that I know many people want is the ability to vote on worlds in some way, not only to keep track of what worlds you like or think are good while keeping your favorites list clean, but also as a source of feedback for creators and a way for VRChat to display popular worlds easier. I do understand the risk of \"dislike bombing,\" but that doesn't seem to be very common anymore.\n\nTwo systems that could be used: The basic like/dislike system or a 5 star rating system. Either one would work well. Just make sure we have a way to see what we thought of it as well as what everyone else thinks. Please don't pull a youtube and hide the dislikes. That feedback is really important for all users.\n\nAlso being able to see your own vote when looking at the world info page would tell you if you've been to a world in the past and what you thought of it. Maybe even hovering over your vote to see when you voted so you can see if the world was updated after you voted. Clicking on the vote could let you change your vote if you accidentally voted or if you changed your mind.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "The ability to like and dislike or vote on worlds.",
